Leonard, I was wrong.

270
00:12:54,390 --> 00:12:56,600
Heaven does exist.

271
00:12:57,290 --> 00:12:59,210
And it's in the basement of a urologist's house

272
00:12:59,210 --> 00:13:01,260
in Sherman Oaks.

273
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:05,940
Welcome to my Fortress of Solitude.

274
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,390
This is where I go to get away from...

275
00:13:09,350 --> 00:13:12,330
all my other solitude.

276
00:13:13,450 --> 00:13:15,560
Oh, come on. It's a replica.

277
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,740
Original.

278
00:13:17,490 --> 00:13:20,180
Oh, I think I just cheated on my wife.

279
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:24,860
The gun from Hellboy?

280
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:25,640
Yup.

281
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,870
How did you get it?

282
00:13:26,870 --> 00:13:28,030
Bought it at auction.

283
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:30,080
Oh, I was hoping for a juicy tidbit

284
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,700
about Ron Perlman's testicles.

285
00:13:34,390 --> 00:13:36,770
Oliver! I'm going to play bingo!

286
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:39,010
Okay, Mother. Have fun.

287
00:13:39,010 --> 00:13:40,150
Still lives with his mom.

288
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:41,940
Yikes, right?

289
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:47,170
Yeah, I'm not quite sure how to respond.

290
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,290
Wow, Donkey Kong!

291
00:13:50,290 --> 00:13:52,690
This-this was my game when I was a kid!

292
00:13:52,690 --> 00:13:55,070
Because it's a story of a pretty blonde girl

293
00:13:55,070 --> 00:13:58,760
tirelessly pursued by a small, oddly-shaped man?

294
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:03,350
No, because I liked it.

295
00:14:03,350 --> 00:14:05,330
Well, now, don't get defensive.

296
00:14:05,330 --> 00:14:08,710
You're oddly-shaped, but you got the girl.

297
00:14:10,330 --> 00:14:12,140
So, I've noticed Leonard gets teased a lot

298
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:14,320
about his relationship with Penny.

299
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:16,660
Yes. If you'd like to join in,

300
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:20,970
the premise is their love seems unlikely and doomed to failure.

301
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,470
So, you think she'll be single soon?

302
00:14:24,470 --> 00:14:26,390
Oh, if you want to get in on the pool,

303
00:14:26,390 --> 00:14:27,760
you're too late...

304
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:30,700
All the squares have been purchased.

305
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,520
Interesting.

306
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:35,180
Excuse me, I have to take care of something.

307
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:46,630
Leonard, as your friend I feel

308
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:49,160
- I should tell you something. - What?

309
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,950
I'm still upset about that peanut sauce.

310
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,160
Oh, could you hold the door?

311
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:59,190
- Nice flowers. - Thank you.

312
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:00,300
They're for a girl.

313
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:03,270
Uh, I'm being implacable and relentless.

314
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,800
Isn't she lucky?

315
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,230
She keeps sending me mixed signals.

316
00:15:10,230 --> 00:15:12,800
But I-I think we both want the same thing.

317
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:13,790
What's that?

318
00:15:13,790 --> 00:15:15,740
Unconditional love.

319
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,390
I guess that's all anybody wants.

320
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:19,610
I guess so.

321
00:15:19,610 --> 00:15:22,930
Well, I hope you get it.

322
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:25,570
One Mississippi, two Mississippi.

323
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:35,480
Next game, let's switch helmets.

324
00:15:36,230 --> 00:15:38,480
No, I'd look silly in that helmet.

325
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:45,810
I-I can't take these.

326
00:15:45,810 --> 00:15:46,870
Well, why not?

327
00:15:46,870 --> 00:15:48,320
I mean, you want what I want.

328
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:51,210
And we had two wonderful Mississippis.

329
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,480
But what about the other girl?

330
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,400
Oh, right.

331
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:59,950
I'll tell her we should just be friends.

332
00:16:06,290 --> 00:16:07,590
Dr. Lorvis?

333
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:10,370
Penny, we should just be friends.

334
00:16:12,090 --> 00:16:13,970
Happy?

335
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:25,090
You think he bites?

336
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,840
Stick your hand in there and find out.

337
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,550
You fooled me with that goat at the petting zoo.

338
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:33,470
You will not fool me again.

339
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,830
I wonder where Dr. Lorvis is.

340
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:38,250
He's been gone a while.

341
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:41,320
Maybe he's playing bingo with his mommy.

342
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:45,880
It's sad how some guys can't cut the apron strings.

343
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,480
Okay, now you're messing with me.

344
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:53,930
Uh, guys, we're locked in here.

345
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:57,150
Oh, this day just keeps getting better!

346
00:17:00,990 --> 00:17:04,180
So, you just left them alone playing games in your house?

347
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:06,130
Well, they seemed happy and...

348
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,130
I thought that would give me time

349
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:10,760
for you and I to get to know each other better.

350
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,390
That was before we met.

351
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,730
We all have a past.

352
00:17:21,050 --> 00:17:22,360
Doc, you've got to see what you're doing

353
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:24,070
is-is a little creepy.

354
00:17:24,070 --> 00:17:25,720
You sound just like Sigourney Weaver

355
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:28,400
when I followed her into a restroom.

356
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:31,460
Okay, you can't just go chasing after

357
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:33,140
every girl who's nice to you.

358
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:35,000
Well, that's not what Sheldon says.

359
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,630
And he seems to know his way around the ladies.

360
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:45,360
Hey, Leonard. Guess who's back! Dr. Lorvis!

361
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,370
Yeah. You care to join us?

362
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:48,420
What?!

363
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:50,660
You locked them in your basement?!

364
00:17:51,390 --> 00:17:53,230
Well, they're, they're not locked in.

365
00:17:53,230 --> 00:17:54,810
The door just sticks.

366
00:17:54,810 --> 00:17:57,530
Okay, so how do they unstick it?

367
00:17:57,530 --> 00:17:59,860
They'd need the key.

368
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:03,510
Okay.

369
00:18:03,510 --> 00:18:04,710
Nope. That's it.

370
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:06,560
We are gonna go over there right now.

371
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:08,620
And you are going to let them out.

372
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:11,670
- Three Mississippi, four Mississippi... - Move it!

373
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:17,740
Oh, good, you're here.

374
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:19,750
Amy, I am so sorry.

375
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:21,520
That has to wait. This weirdo locked

376
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:23,400
- the guys up in his basement. - What?!

377
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,000
- She seems nice. Who's she? - Just walk.

378
00:18:32,190 --> 00:18:33,480
You can do this.

379
00:18:34,490 --> 00:18:35,820
One ladder left!

380
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,530
- Oh-ho! Yeah! - Yes!

381
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:39,470
Next level!

382
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:41,450
- Leonard, are you okay? - Better than okay.

383
00:18:41,450 --> 00:18:44,110
I am having the game of my life!

384
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:48,010
Dr. Lorvis, isn't there something you want to say?

385
00:18:48,010 --> 00:18:48,620
Yes.

386
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:50,910
I'm very sorry for locking you in my home.

387
00:18:50,910 --> 00:18:52,200
Yeah, that was very uncool.

388
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,370
Get the hammer! Get the hammer!

389
00:18:53,370 --> 00:18:54,500
Got it.

390
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,640
Okay, Leonard, let's go!

391
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,640
J-Just hang on!

392
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,590
Well, while we wait,

393
00:19:02,590 --> 00:19:06,440
would you like to see Tobey Maguire's prostate sonogram?

394
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:08,390
Sure. Yeah.

395
00:19:08,390 --> 00:19:09,820
Oh, spoiler alert.

396
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:12,450
Uh, he was worried about nothing.

